The distributed XCPCIO assets are built from the scoreboard-only source fork
under upstream/xcpcio-board-app-scoreboard-only. The fork removes the rating,
statistics, Resolver, Balloon, and Countdown implementations and removes
Highcharts, highcharts-vue, and GSAP before compilation. The official XCPCIO
prebuilt bundle is not included. The exact patch, build record, MIT license,
and runtime dependency notices are retained under upstream and
public/hydro-league-xcpcio.

The `league-xcpcio` name, same-origin Hydro proxy, access-control boundary,
offline wrapper, source fork, and self-hosted assets were added in 2026 by
Hydro League Sync contributors. Existing Hydro `xcpcio` routes are not
replaced.

The release package bundles the locked runtime dependencies `@react-spring/*`,
`schemastery`, and their transitive dependencies for offline installation.
Their package metadata and license files are retained under `node_modules` in
the release tarball. React, React DOM, and Hydro remain host-provided peers and
are not bundled.

The school badge files named `besti.png`, `buct.jpg`, and `muc.png` under
`public/hydro-league-xcpcio/school-badges` were provided by the contest
organizer solely for organization identification. Ownership and trademark rights
remain with the respective schools. These badge files are not licensed under
the AGPL. Each deployer must ensure it has authorization to use them and may
replace or remove them for its deployment.

